# Workspace Venv Fallback and Sync

## Fallback: use workspace venv when repo venv fails

If a repo's local `.venv` is broken or missing, use the workspace venv:
```bash
source /home/hk/unified-trading-system-repos/.venv-workspace/bin/activate
```
The workspace venv has all unified libraries installed and works across all repos.

## Sync: keep both venvs aligned when pyproject.toml changes

When you update a repo's `pyproject.toml` (add/remove/update dependencies):
1. Install in the repo venv: `cd <repo> && uv pip install -e ".[dev]"`
2. Install in the workspace venv: `cd /home/hk/unified-trading-system-repos && uv pip install -e "<repo>/[dev]"`
3. Commit `uv.lock` with your changes (quickmerge handles this automatically)

NEVER: manually create venvs outside of `uv`; use `pip install` instead of `uv pip install`
